.THS Checkgroups 5L News.SH NAMECheckgroups - a list of newsgroups to be affected by a checkgroupscontrol message..SH DESCRIPTION.ti +3If a checkgroups control message is received then this file is used tolimit the newsgroups to be checked, so it is avoided that all groups arechecked when a local (or other limited) checkgroups control messagearrived..SH FORMAT.ti +3Each line of the file contains one limitation of the form.ce<dist>   <group>{,<group>}where.B <dist>is the distribution of this control message and.B <group>is a newsgroup expression on which this checkgroups is limited. In.B <group>there are the wildcards.B ?and.B *allowed (as known by the shell)..SH EXAMPLE.raw 4sub      sub.*muc      muc.*local    local*world    rec.*,comp.*,talk.*,news.*,misc.*.noraw